Firmware images
---------------

In `firmware/`, the EEPROM contents in `firmware/eeprom/`.

Read-only images of the instruments' own program ROMs, from which the
SCPI command tree in `docs/scpi/z3801a.md` was extracted and against
which claims about the command set are checked.  CPU32 code, big-endian, loaded at address zero; see
`docs/firmware/` for which part.

  z3801a-3543.bin            Z3801A firmware, revision 3543.  Copyright
                             Hewlett-Packard 1993.  Identical, byte for
                             byte, to the ROM of the bench Z3801A read
                             back through its console (`docs/firmware/`).
  z3816a-4001.bin            Z3816A firmware, revision 4001.  Copyright
                             Hewlett-Packard 2000.
  58503a-3633.bin            58503A firmware, revision 3633.  Copyright
                             Hewlett-Packard 1993.  Assembled from the
                             four AM29F010 dumps published by willhb at
                             github.com/willhb/HP-58503A-Firmware
                             (58503_80007..80010_RevA, labeled 2L, 1L,
                             2M and 1M).  Each pair is interleaved byte
                             by byte, the M part on the even bytes, and
                             pair 1 is the low half: the order the reset
                             vector at address 0 (stack `0x10fffe`,
                             entry `0x550`) and the boot checksums
                             settle, and what `smartclock-cli
                             join-chips` does.

  58503a-3704.bin            58503A firmware, revision 3704.  Copyright
                             Hewlett-Packard 1993.  Read on 2026-09-26
                             through the pForth console of the bench
                             58503A, serial 3710A01056, which answers
                             *IDN? with 3704-C (`docs/firmware/`,
                             "Reading memory through it").  512 KB from
                             address 0; SHA-256 d13b9ff1...9491ca3.
                             Identical, byte for byte, to a set of
                             four AM29F010 dumps labeled "U11..U14
                             58503-00007..10", files dated 2018-10-08,
                             posted as "Firmware Unknown" to the
                             HP-Agilent-Keysight-equipment group,
                             groups.io/g/HP-Agilent-Keysight-equipment/
                             topic/121519426, alongside willhb's RevA
                             set, and forwarded by Daniel Straus on
                             2026-10-07.  Joined as the 3633 image is;
                             not kept here, since they add nothing to
                             the image.  Where they were read is not
                             known.

  z3805a-3543b.bin           Z3805A firmware, revision 3543B.  Copyright
                             Hewlett-Packard 1993.  Read on 2026-09-27
                             through the pForth console of the bench
                             Z3805A, serial 3625A01487, which answers
                             *IDN? with 3543B-A.  512 KB from address 0;
                             SHA-256 216daf92...f6998792.

  z3815a-4010.bin            Z3815A firmware, revision U-4010.0.
                             Copyright Hewlett-Packard 1993.  Its GPS
                             engine is a Furuno GT-74, spoken to in
                             Furuno's $PFEC sentences, not an Oncore.
                             Posted as Z3815A_Rev_4010.zip by Razvan
                             Popescu to the HP-Agilent-Keysight-equipment
                             group on 2026-10-04, groups.io/g/
                             HP-Agilent-Keysight-equipment/message/159758,
                             with Z3801A 3543 and Z3816A 4001 images
                             identical to the ones above.  How it was
                             read is not stated.  Its word sum, the
                             Z3816A's, holds.  SHA-256 5aa9083d...0968e80.

  58503b-1.01.04.bin         58503B firmware, revision 1.01.04.
                             Copyright Hewlett-Packard 1993.  Rebuilt
                             here from 58503b-L85376-console.log, the
                             console of a 58503B, serial L85376, which
                             answers *IDN? with 1.01.04-D, posted as
                             pForth_Console_Buffer.tar.gz by Razvan
                             Popescu to the same group on 2026-10-05,
                             groups.io/g/HP-Agilent-Keysight-equipment/
                             message/159781.  The log enters the
                             console with :SYST:LANG "PFORTH" and prints
                             all 512 KB from address 0, an address and
                             256 bytes to a line, in hex without leading
                             zeros.  All 2048 lines are present, in
                             order, with 256 values each, and the
                             image's word sum, the Z3816A's rule rather
                             than the 58503A's lane sums, holds.
                             SHA-256 2ea754e9...ac521dd4.

  58503b-L85376-console.log  That console log, as posted.  The first
                             part is the poster's terminal tests.
                             SHA-256 b4be1ed8...1c9a6be5.

EEPROM contents, read the same way, 8 KB from `0x400000` (chip select
9).  Each holds that unit's settings, calibration and diagnostic log:

  58503a-3710A01056-eeprom.bin  the bench 58503A, 3704-C.
  z3801a-3542A01548-eeprom.bin  the bench Z3801A, 3543-A.
  z3805a-3625A01487-eeprom.bin  the bench Z3805A, 3543B-A.

The revision is the string the firmware puts in the third field of its
`*IDN?` answer, stored just before the image's second copyright notice
(`0x12eee` in the Z3801A image, `0x22ff8` in the Z3816A's, `0x12fea` in
the 58503A 3633's, `0x1309c` in the 3704's, `0x12eee` in the Z3805A
3543B's, `0x23090` in the Z3815A's, `0x2307c` in the 58503B's).  The letter
that follows it in a real answer, as in 3704-C, is read from RAM and is
not in the image.

